sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Materials as MaterialsPanel.tsx (subject "Materials")
    participant AppData as AppDataProvider (lib/store/app-data.tsx)
    participant LS as localStorage ("asa.data.v2")
    participant Assistant as AssistantChat.tsx (general assistant attachments)
    participant Storage as Storage bucket: chat-attachments
    participant DB as Supabase (assistant_attachments)

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over Materials,LS: Subject "Materials" panel — study-material metadata is<br/>local prototype state only, not uploaded to Supabase Storage today.
    User->>Materials: add a material (name, type, section, subject, url/notes)
    Materials->>AppData: addMaterial(input)
    AppData->>LS: persist DataState (materials[]) to localStorage
    end

    rect rgb(245,245,245)
    Note over Assistant,DB: General Assistant attachments ARE real Supabase uploads.
    User->>Assistant: attach a file to an assistant message
    Assistant->>Assistant: validateAttachment(file) — 1 MiB limit for image/audio/video,<br/>PDF/DOCX otherwise
    Assistant->>Storage: upload to chat-attachments/<uid>/...
    Assistant->>DB: insert assistant_attachments row (parse_status: "unparsed")
    end

    Note over DB: BACKEND TODO FOR CODEX: there is no separate "study document"<br/>ingestion pipeline invoked by the frontend. The `documents` /<br/>`document_chunks` tables referenced by storage-management.ts are read<br/>defensively for storage accounting only; nothing in the frontend<br/>writes to them.
